From 0641fd3158465376c013f81f08e1e01a58b3da4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 14sea <wanhuaning@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 17 May 2026 08:35:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?Phase=206.0:=20drop=20KEY2=20from=20reset=20pat?=
 =?UTF-8?q?h=20=E2=80=94=20un-stick=20first-boot?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

AX301 has no external pull-up on KEY2 (pin E16).  The previous attempt
(set_instance_assignment WEAK_PULL_UP_RESISTOR ON, qsf-only) was rejected
by the Quartus 21.1 fitter:

  Error (169057): Can't place I/O pin KEY2 at pin location E16 -- I/O
                  pin uses weak pullup, which is not supported by this
                  pin location.

That earlier 0006 was committed without an actual Quartus build — the
silicon-validated 2026-05-17 .pof predated the commit by 4 minutes and
was built off a one-shot RTL bypass that was never persisted.  This
commit ships that bypass: drop KEY2 from rstn_int entirely so the POR
counter alone releases reset.

Cost: KEY2 no longer works as a manual reset button (power-cycle or
re-JTAG-load instead).  Acceptable for ROT bring-up — the board has no
working reset button anyway without an external pull-up resistor.

Verified empirically Phase 6 bring-up 2026-05-17: with rstn_int <=
por_cnt(3), stage2 prints its full boot trace + waits in the dispatcher
exactly as expected.
---
 rtl/ax301_top.vhd | 17 +++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/rtl/ax301_top.vhd b/rtl/ax301_top.vhd
index a253b05..6e8573e 100644
--- a/rtl/ax301_top.vhd
+++ b/rtl/ax301_top.vhd
@@ -178,19 +178,24 @@ architecture rtl of ax301_top is
 
 begin
 
-  -- ── Power-on reset (same pattern as riscv_demo soc_top.v) ─────────────────
-  -- Hold reset for 8 cycles after KEY2 goes high.
+  -- ── Power-on reset ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+  -- AX301 has no external pull-up on KEY2 and Cyclone IV E pin E16 doesn't
+  -- support internal WEAK_PULL_UP_RESISTOR (Quartus 21.1 fitter rejects it),
+  -- so the original "rstn_int <= KEY2 and por_cnt(3)" wedges at 0 whenever
+  -- the user isn't actively holding KEY2 — CPU never leaves reset, stage2
+  -- silent on UART.  Bring-up 2026-05-17 confirmed empirically.  Drop KEY2
+  -- from the reset path; the POR counter alone releases reset 8 cycles
+  -- after CLOCK is stable.  Cost: KEY2 no longer functions as a manual
+  -- reset (use power-cycle or re-JTAG-load to reset).
   por: process(CLOCK)
   begin
     if rising_edge(CLOCK) then
-      if KEY2 = '0' then
-        por_cnt <= (others => '0');
-      elsif por_cnt(3) = '0' then
+      if por_cnt(3) = '0' then
         por_cnt <= std_ulogic_vector(unsigned(por_cnt) + 1);
       end if;
     end if;
   end process;
-  rstn_int <= KEY2 and por_cnt(3);
+  rstn_int <= por_cnt(3);
 
   -- ── NEORV32 processor ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   neorv32_top_inst: neorv32_top
-- 
